# Template for the one secret this tool can use: an Apify API token.
# It is needed only by `sync`, and only to fetch the track list of a playlist that is
# not cached yet. Lyrics, audio, playback and the overlay need no secret.
#
# `sync` reads it from the APIFY_TOKEN environment variable. Never commit a real value.
# Two ways to supply it:
#
#   * Put the line below, filled in, in a `.env` file in the directory you run from
#     (`.env` is gitignored), or
#   * keep it outside the repo, for example in ~/.config/playlist-player/secrets.env
#     (mode 600), and export it for the one command that needs it:
#
#       set -a; . ~/.config/playlist-player/secrets.env; set +a
#       python -m playlist_player sync '<playlist url>'
#
#     Prefer this when other accounts or automated tools can read the repo directory.
#
# Get a token from the Apify Console under Settings -> API & Integrations.
APIFY_TOKEN=
